stxlib::glyphs, the font reader

The font reader of stxlib::glyphs (include/stxlib/font_file.hpp and
src/algorithms/glyphs/font_file.cpp, font_truetype.cpp, font_cff.cpp,
font_reader.hpp) is part of STXlib and is STXlib's own code, under STXlib's
licence (the repository's LICENSE). It is a conversion to house-style C++
of the design of two projects, each offered under the MIT licence or the
Apache License 2.0; it is taken under the MIT licence, and carries their
notices, which follow unchanged.

- ttf-parser 0.25.1 (https://github.com/harfbuzz/ttf-parser), by Yevhenii
  Reizner: the table directory and collections, the face's numbers, the
  character maps, advances, a glyph's range in glyf and the two passes over
  a simple glyph's flags and coordinates, the indexes and dictionaries of
  CFF and the operators of its charstrings.
- Skrifa 0.50.0 and read-fonts 0.47.0 (https://github.com/googlefonts/
  fontations), by the Fontations developers: a composite glyph put together
  in whole numbers, the outline placed by its left side bearing, a scaled
  glyph's parts scaled on their own, and a CFF glyph's coordinates in whole
  font units with the lines and points that are left out.

The rasterizer of stxlib::glyphs (glyph_mask.hpp, mask.cpp, chords.hpp,
flatten.hpp, centres.hpp, reciprocal.hpp) is not a conversion of either.

